{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats","id":1558988,"title":"Frenzy feats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-24T06:16:12-07:00","id":1558988,"title":"Frenzy feats","content":"Is ti tintended for vampires to be the strongest spalt (STR wise)?<br /> If a vamp frenzies he adds his blood potency to the rolls. That means a 5 BP vamp gets +5 lets add +5 from vigour, blood buff and maybe some colis to control the frenzy and we have a monster. If we add riding the wave combat style the BP bonus doubles for an action. Is this intended? Werewolves cant even compare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T09:09:36-07:00","id":1558993,"title":"","content":"The Riding The Wave Style Merit doesn't double the Strength bonus for regular attacks against non-object targets. Physical Intensity is an explosive burst of power that only adds to rolls instead of the Attribute, lasts one turn, and is less efficient than Disciplines in terms of Vitae cost when Vitae is disproportionately important to vampires compared to other monsters' fuel traits. Even with the Coil of the Wyrm, riding the wave requires rolls.<br /> <br /> For comparison:<br /> <br /> Gauru form gives werewolves +3 Strength by default and Favored Form allows that to go up by another dot (with a Rank 3 Totem giving enough of an effective Experience budget to give every member of the pack another Attribute dot plus a one-dot Merit) in addition to Primal Strength adding Purity to the Attribute. This costs no Essence and doesn't require them to accumulate successes on controlled frenzy, with the turn limit and risk of Death Rage being the primary concerns.<br /> <br /> The ceiling on Honing the Form from Mage is technically as high as they can offset the spell factor penalties for the cost of a point of Mana to break the Trait limit, with a maxed-out Rote Skill and a soul stone tool alone allowing +5 Strength without any net penalty to the base casting pool \u2014 a starting mage with minor investment can pull this off handily, to say nothing of a character at Gnosis 5.<br /> <br /> A Promethean with the Unconquered Alembic adds their Azoth to their Strength rating as a free passive effect, enabling an Azoth 10 Promethean to have a Strength of 20 before any expenditures for Transhuman Potential. This costs no Experiences unless the character wants to retain access to the effect after changing Refinements. The same Alembic also allows them to lift and throw massive objects in a way that Vigor doesn't facilitate.<br /> <br /> Deviants with Superhuman Strength can just outright set their minimum Strength rating to 8 if it's under 3 (or add +5 flat), and while the cost by default is a commensurate Scar there are multiple workarounds \u2014 even just going from the corebook, Cephalists and Coactives can boost the Magnitude of their Variations and Chimerics can drop their Scars' Magnitude to the level of pure roleplaying incentives, and Shallow Graves provides means of using Acclimation as the basis for further widening the gap between effect and cost.<br /> <br /> tl;dr The Kindred can put a lot of resources toward being able to use physical power on their environment, but it's generally wildly inefficient to do so on a prolonged basis and many other monsters can manage more stable results with less investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-26T22:30:01-07:00","id":1559039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats#post1558988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is ti tintended for vampires to be the strongest spalt (STR wise)?<br /> If a vamp frenzies he adds his blood potency to the rolls. That means a 5 BP vamp gets +5 lets add +5 from vigour, blood buff and maybe some colis to control the frenzy and we have a monster. If we add riding the wave combat style the BP bonus doubles for an action. Is this intended? Werewolves cant even compare.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The trade off is that while you are Frenzied, you are too delerious to use anything more complicated than physical disciplines.<br /> <br /> That means no mind control and no blood magic. Just full 'unga bunga,' and you're in trouble if that's not enough to get the job done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-27T11:15:44-07:00","id":1559046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559039#post1559039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The trade off is that while you are Frenzied, you are too delerious to use anything more complicated than physical disciplines.<br /> <br /> That means no mind control and no blood magic. Just full 'unga bunga,' and you're in trouble if that's not enough to get the job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my view, no: the rules do not say that in frenzy you can only use physical Disciplines. They say something else, namely that during frenzy the rational mind is no longer in command and the Beast wants to solve the immediate problem, basically by any means necessary. So the real point is not \u201cphysical yes, mental no.\u201d<br /> <br /> The point is that whatever Discipline you use has to be consistent with the Beast\u2019s impulse in that moment. If it helps you hunt, overwhelm, terrify, reach the prey, break through an obstacle, or unleash rage, then I think it fits. If it requires calm thinking, subtle manipulation, long planning, or self-control, then it does not.<br /> That is why I do not think mental Disciplines are automatically off the table in frenzy. They just stop being refined tools and become extensions of the Beast.<br /> <br /> For example, Dominate. If the vampire is in hunger frenzy and the prey has locked itself behind a door, I see no reason why the Beast could not fix on the nearest person and spit out a single brutal command: \u201cOpen.\u201d That is not elegant mind control. It is the Beast using the shortest possible path to get to the prey.<br /> <br /> Same with a vampire who is being restrained, pinned down, or held in place while thrashing in frenzy. A sharp \u201cFree me\u201d or \u201cLet go\u201d feels completely in line with the state. Again, not subtle, not strategic, just raw predatory will smashing through an obstacle.<br /> <br /> Majesty also makes sense to me in that context, just not as a composed social performance. Imagine a frenzied vampire surrounded by people trying to corner him. He does not speak, does not negotiate, does not seduce in any human sense. He simply imposes himself. His presence becomes monstrous, almost demonic, like a succubus or some infernal predator pressing down on everyone in the room. People freeze, recoil, lose their nerve, look away, or instinctively back off. That is still Majesty, but expressed as pure supernatural presence rather than deliberate charm.<br /> <br /> So for me the correct reading is: mental Disciplines do not vanish in frenzy; they are only limited by the Beast\u2019s immediate drive. If they serve that drive, they work. If they require the vampire to act against it, or with too much lucidity and finesse, then they do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T13:55:46-07:00","id":1559072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559046#post1559046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So for me the correct reading is: mental Disciplines do not vanish in frenzy; they are only limited by the Beast\u2019s immediate drive. If they serve that drive, they work. If they require the vampire to act against it, or with too much lucidity and finesse, then they do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consistently see the Beast referred to as <i>&quot;a wild animal&quot;</i> in regards to how it behaves.<br /> <br /> In every game I've come across where a Wight is present, they were reduced to a bunch of snarling zombies, who lacked the capacity for even the most rudimentary speech.<br /> <br /> Basically just throwing themselves at their nearest victim, until somebody got lucky enough to put them down for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T17:20:41-07:00","id":1559078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559072#post1559072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I consistently see the Beast referred to as <i>&quot;a wild animal&quot;</i> in regards to how it behaves.<br /> <br /> In every game I've come across where a Wight is present, they were reduced to a bunch of snarling zombies, who lacked the capacity for even the most rudimentary speech.<br /> <br /> Basically just throwing themselves at their nearest victim, until somebody got lucky enough to put them down for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lecit way to play it, but not by raw. Corebook states: &quot;... Beast is not stupid&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's driven by its primal urges, but disciplines are the very manifestation of the Beast. I see much more interesting to have a frenzy vampire using them as a primeval manifestation of it's true nature. Without caring about Masquerade, life or anything else if not pursing its desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T21:06:17-07:00","id":1559079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559078#post1559078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's driven by its primal urges, but disciplines are the very manifestation of the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nay, disciplines were a form of magic that Lilith obtained from demons and angels. She passed the secrets onto Caine, who then passed them onto his own descendants.<br /> <br /> Originally, Caine's curse was just to be a night dwelling, blood sucking monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T22:20:13-07:00","id":1559083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559072#post1559072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In every game I've come across where a Wight is present, they were reduced to a bunch of snarling zombies, who lacked the capacity for even the most rudimentary speech.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559079#post1559079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nay, disciplines were a form of magic that Lilith obtained from demons and angels. She passed the secrets onto Caine, who then passed them onto his own descendants.<br /> <br /> Originally, Caine's curse was just to be a night dwelling, blood sucking monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I don't agree that speech-based uses of Dominate are beyond the scope of consideration for a vampire in the grip of frenzy, but you're referencing Masquerade concepts in a Requiem thread. Caine is a memetic reference to an old Longinian heresy in this game rather than any sort of proven Kindred progenitor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T00:22:35-07:00","id":1559085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559079#post1559079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nay, disciplines were a form of magic that Lilith obtained from demons and angels. She passed the secrets onto Caine, who then passed them onto his own descendants.<br /> <br /> Originally, Caine's curse was just to be a night dwelling, blood sucking monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Masquerade <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As said. To me also mental discipline are allowed in a primordial, feral, bestial way.<br /> Also with dominate: a hissed command like: come to me. Open. Rip out his throat. Are all valid in case there're no other means to reach out the objective.<br /> That incoude also if the frenzied vampire is overwhelmed by enemies he cannot stands.<br /> <br /> Again:<br /> - Beast isn't stupid (p. 104)<br /> - A frenzying vampire can, but is under no compulsion to, lash out with her predatory aura (p. 103). Which include all the auras - also Competitive (which uses intelligence) and Seductive (which uses Presence) ones - not only monstous - and Majesty or dominate are an extention of these auras.<br /> <br /> And more than that, also from a balance point of view: it will be almost a huge advantage to go in frenzy if the PC is vigor based rather than mental/social based. Making a frenzied vampire with only mental discipline almost a joke compared to someone with high vigor/celerity.<br /> <br /> That been said, whatever works best for your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-29-2026, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T07:45:18-07:00","id":1559091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559085#post1559085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more than that, also from a balance point of view: it will be almost a huge advantage to go in frenzy if the PC is vigor based rather than mental/social based. Making a frenzied vampire with only mental discipline almost a joke compared to someone with high vigor/celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy is a liability first and a physical buff second to make it so that the mental/social-based character going into frenzy is still a physical danger to their surroundings as far as most mortals are concerned because it wouldn't be great Vampire Drama if your overwhelming bloodlust still allowed you to make intelligent decisions.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the clan most associated with frenzy is the one that has a reputation for dwelling in wild places where people don't go and only has Animalism as a non-bodily Discipline. From a balance point of view, if you want frenzy to be a super mode for a character you build toward things that are advantages in frenzy.<br /> <br /> Characters who specialize their Predatory Aura toward one of the aspects over the other two still have access to those modes of imposition, but you wouldn't expect the character who's specced into the Competitive Beast to roll well invoking the Monstrous Beast outside their territory just because frenzy permits you to pursue your drive in ways that aren't wholly suicidal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T09:22:38-07:00","id":1559093,"title":"","content":"Go for it. As I said, it's a lecit interpretation.<br /> I wiill personally stick to the corebook statements:<br /> - Beast isn't stupid. Which means has a kind of intelligence.<br /> - will do wathever to end the problem by any means necessary. Which also suggest to me it's not dumb, and any useful means it can be used regardless character's morality.<br /> <br /> To me Frenzy is that your character is taken by the Beast who only pursue its driver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-29-2026, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T11:19:02-07:00","id":1559096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1558988-frenzy-feats?p=1559083#post1559083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but you're referencing Masquerade concepts in a Requiem thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops! Seems I overlooked that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}